      "heading": "Jenkins - Interview Questions and Practical Answers",
      "explanation": "## Introduction\nJenkins is an automation server used to build, test and deploy applications. A Jenkins pipeline describes the steps needed to move code from source control to a deployable release.\n\n## Architecture\nThe controller manages jobs, credentials, plugins and scheduling. Agents execute build tasks. Jenkinsfiles define pipeline stages. Credentials are stored in Jenkins credentials management and should be exposed only to the required steps.\n\n## End-to-End Workflow\nA Git webhook starts a pipeline. Jenkins checks out code, installs dependencies, runs tests, builds an artifact or image, scans it, publishes it and deploys to the target environment. Each stage reports success or failure.\n\n## Interview Question\nA Jenkins pipeline remains in the queue and never starts. What do you check?\n\n## Detailed Answer\nInspect the queue reason and required agent label. Check whether matching agents are online and have free executors. Review agent provisioning, cloud capacity, controller logs and agent connection logs. Check whether a node is temporarily offline or restricted. Do not increase executors blindly when the machine is already overloaded.\n\n## Production Troubleshooting\nNo executor: check queue and node labels. Agent offline: check network, Java compatibility and agent logs. Pipeline syntax error: validate Jenkinsfile. Plugin issue: check plugin compatibility and controller logs. Secret unavailable: check credential ID and scope. Back up JENKINS_HOME.",
