      "heading": "Ansible - Interview Questions and Practical Answers",
      "explanation": "## Introduction\nAnsible automates server configuration and application setup. It connects to managed machines, runs tasks and helps keep systems in the required state.\n\n## Architecture\nThe control node runs Ansible. Inventory lists managed hosts and groups. Playbooks contain plays and tasks. Modules perform work on remote systems. Roles organize reusable tasks, templates, files, variables and handlers.\n\n## End-to-End Workflow\nCreate inventory. Define variables. Write a playbook using suitable modules. Run syntax checks. Test in check mode or staging. Apply to a limited group first. Verify the result and run again to confirm idempotency.\n\n## Interview Question\nA playbook reports changed every time even when nothing appears to change. Why?\n\n## Detailed Answer\nA shell or command task may always report changed unless it has suitable creates, removes or changed_when conditions. A template may contain changing timestamps or unstable values. Prefer declarative modules such as package, copy, template and service. Run the playbook twice and confirm the second run reports no unnecessary changes.\n\n## Production Troubleshooting\nUnreachable host: verify SSH, DNS, port and key. Permission denied: check remote user and become settings. Repeated changed status: inspect command tasks and template values. Wrong variable: check precedence and inventory group membership. Test against a small host group before broad rollout.",
