      "heading": "ArgoCD - Interview Questions and Practical Answers",
      "explanation": "## Introduction\nArgo CD is a GitOps continuous delivery tool for Kubernetes. It watches the desired application configuration in Git and compares it with the live cluster.\n\n## Architecture\nThe API server provides the interface. The repository server reads Git repositories and renders manifests. The application controller compares desired and live state and performs reconciliation. Applications connect repositories to destination clusters and namespaces.\n\n## End-to-End Workflow\nStore Kubernetes YAML or Helm charts in Git. Create an Argo CD Application. Argo CD reads the repository and compares it with the cluster. A developer merges a change. Argo CD detects the change and syncs it according to the configured policy.\n\n## Interview Question\nArgo CD shows an application as OutOfSync. How do you investigate?\n\n## Detailed Answer\nOpen the application diff and compare Git manifests with live resources. Identify whether someone changed the cluster manually, a controller changed a field, or Git contains a new desired version. Decide which state is correct. Fix the source in Git and sync through the approved process. Review prune and self-heal settings before enabling them.\n\n## Production Troubleshooting\nOutOfSync: inspect diff and live drift. Sync failed: inspect repository rendering, permissions, API errors and events. App missing resources: verify path, target revision and namespace. Health degraded: inspect the affected Kubernetes resources and their events.",
