      "heading": "Prometheus - Interview Questions and Practical Answers",
      "explanation": "## Introduction\nPrometheus collects time-series metrics from applications and infrastructure. Teams use it to understand system health, create alerts and investigate performance problems.\n\n## Architecture\nPrometheus periodically scrapes metrics endpoints. It stores timestamped samples with labels. PromQL queries the data. Recording rules precompute useful queries. Alerting rules send firing alerts to Alertmanager for routing and notification.\n\n## End-to-End Workflow\nExpose application metrics. Configure scrape targets. Confirm targets are healthy. Build PromQL queries. Create recording and alerting rules. Route alerts through Alertmanager. Review retention and storage capacity.\n\n## Interview Question\nA Prometheus target is DOWN. What do you check?\n\n## Detailed Answer\nRead the exact scrape error on the Targets page. Test the metrics endpoint from the Prometheus network context. Check DNS, routing, firewall rules, port, metrics path, TLS, authentication and exporter health. Verify service discovery and relabeling have not removed the target.\n\n## Production Troubleshooting\nTarget DOWN: inspect scrape error and network path. No data: verify metric name, labels, time range and scrape status. High memory: inspect retention, series count and cardinality. Alert noise: improve expression, duration, severity and routing. Avoid labels containing user IDs or request IDs.",
